          "english_quote": "she fled with him, went abroad",
          "issue": "“Went abroad” treats the foreign land as a destination, whereas ἐν ἀλλοδαπῇ identifies the location of the action expressed by ὁρμήσασα. On the lodging or anchoring sense of ὁρμέω, she stopped or stayed in a foreign land. Reading the form from ὁρμάω instead would concern setting out or moving there. The draft neither represents this distinction accurately nor discloses the lexical choice.",
