          "source_quote": "οὐκ ἐβουλήθην τὸ καθ’ ὑμᾶς αὐτῷ συναντιβαλεῖν, μέχρις ἂν ὑμῖν προσανάθωμαι.",
          "english_quote": "I did not want to compare your circumstances with his account until I had consulted you.",
          "issue": "The personal dative αὐτῷ identifies the old man as the participant in the proposed exchange. “With his account” substitutes an account for that person and leaves unrepresented Peter’s withholding of a discussion with him. The comparison or exchange expressed by συναντιβαλεῖν must retain this interpersonal element.",
          "suggested_revision": "Proposed wording: “I did not wish to bring up your circumstances with him until I had consulted you.” A note can explain that συναντιβαλεῖν suggests bringing accounts together for comparison in conversation. Review the replacement afresh before accepting it.",
